{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RESOLVED in Gerrit 1406 (not yet landed — do NOT close until Verified +1)\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1406 — `2613827564`, rebased onto `gerrit/main`\n(`7f09a32eaf`) before push.\n\n**Root cause** (runtime-proven, see the RCA comment above): `wait_for_jira_dc_ready` returned on the\nfirst `serverInfo` 200 and never touched `/rest/api/2/field`.\n\n**Fix — one shared definition.** `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py` (new, stdlib-only, injected\ntransport) now owns `REQUIRED_FIELDS`, the bounded budget, the \"unusable or system-only inventory\nmeans NOT-READY, never degraded image\" predicate, and the two-cause failure prose. Both tiers call\nit: `wait_for_jira_dc_ready` keeps the cheap `serverInfo` poll as stage one then waits on the shared\ndefinition under `JIRA_DC_FIELD_READY_TIMEOUT`; the probe's `_await_named_fields` delegates;\n`_assert_project_capabilities` routes its field check through the same wait. Stdlib-only because the\nprobe workflow runs `python scripts/...` with no venv — verified importable under system Python 3.9.\n\n**Criteria.** AC1 met for the harness (`conftest.py:209-219`). AC2 met — `not_ready_message` quotes\nthe observed inventory. AC3 met — the abort names BOTH \"never registered\" and \"does not offer\".\nAC4 met — one definition, pinned by a test that fails if either tier stops routing through it.\nAC5 met — `test_a_system_only_field_inventory_reads_as_not_ready`.\n\n**RED -> GREEN, held out.** Six cells written and observed RED first (`DID NOT RAISE RuntimeError`;\n`declared the instance ready having polled only ['/rest/api/2/serverInfo']`), then moved out of the\ntree before the fixer ran, then GREEN against an oracle it never saw.\n\n**Mutation checks (6).** Re-introducing the exact root cause (return after serverInfo) killed 4\ncells; probe-stops-delegating killed the AC4 cell; dropping \"does not offer\" killed AC3; reverting to\nthe old image-degrade wording killed 2; omitting the inventory dump killed AC2. **One mutation\ninitially SURVIVED** — treating an unusable read as ready — exposing a real gap, so\n`test_an_unreadable_field_inventory_reads_as_not_ready` was added (RED under that mutant, GREEN\nwithout it).\n\n**Gates:** `make lint` exit 0, `make typecheck` exit 0 (433 files),\n`pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal` exit 0 —\n**10234 passed, 38 skipped, 0 failed**. A first run caught `test_comment_hygiene_guard` on a bare\n`9790` next to a CI run id; fixed by citing the full ticket id.\n\n**Parity sweep** found a third live-DC channel that never got this rule —\n`scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py`, which maps the Epic-field contract after the same `serverInfo`\ncurl loop with no field wait, and whose output is the authority a human uses to update\n`_REQUIRED_FIELDS`. Filed as [rebar:4a6d-5bbc-44f4-4a56], linked `discovered_from`.\n\n**Residual risk.** `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py` is now 916 LOC. The CI module-size gate\nscopes to `src/rebar/**/*.py` only (`_build-and-test.yml:291-296`), so this does not fail the build,\nbut the file was already over the 800 guidance before this change. Accepted in scope; a split would\nbe a separate refactor."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785899776940764001,"uuid":"2c44877a-7ef1-436b-babf-fd9bf261a221"}